  "reason": "The current best (config_041: scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, acc=0.7250) has been well-characterized across aggregation and fusion, but the RNA encoder dimension remains untested with this strong pipeline. config_015 showed scgpt is catastrophic (0.52), but pca_n2000 has never been paired with imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted. Testing config_011 (pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted) will clarify whether the RNA encoder is a critical bottleneck or whether the image encoder + transformer aggregation drive most of the performance. If PCA matches scvi_n200, it confirms the pipeline is robust and I can focus remaining budget on fine-tuning; if it falls well short, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and I should exhaust scvi_n200 variants (e.g., singleprofile) in the last 3 experiments. This is the highest-information experiment given the sparse evidence on RNA encoder choice within the top-performing architecture."
}

